CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Awards\, Receptions and Celebrations\,Providenc
 e\,United States
DESCRIPTION:Join us for the opening reception of To Sew with Anger\, a thr
 ee part project bringing together 10 women of color across Massachusetts a
 nd Rhode Island to reflect on the recitations of self-described “Black\,
  lesbian\, mother\, warrior\, poet\,” Audre Lorde. This project draws on
  Lorde’s work to disrupt dominant narratives surrounding process\, artis
 tic creation\, and our emotions. We turn to the erotic\, described as an i
 nternal sense of satisfaction\, power\, and knowledge\, to make sense of t
 he contemporary moment and blur the boundaries of authorship. The opening 
 reception will include a gallery walkthrough and brief remarks from the cu
 rators\, artists\, and participants of the project. ퟿� Friday\, Oct\nC
