BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Film Screening: Raging Bull — Berkeley/San Francisco
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-07:00":20261016T190000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-07:00":20261016T200000
DTSTAMP:20261017T203942Z
UID:028a75c53543c1a9b35988df9516@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Films\,Berkeley/San Francisco\,United States
DESCRIPTION:Martin Scorsese and Robert De Niro make the biography of boxer
  Jake LaMotta into a visceral meditation on existential suffering. Eschewi
 ng the romance associated with the sport\, Raging Bull shows the struggle 
 of an athlete whose willful determination to succeed on his own terms take
 s its toll on all those around him—friends and adversaries in equal meas
 ure—before he is undermined by self-loathing. Every punch is framed\, li
 t\, and cut for maximum impact\, with black-and-white cinematography inspi
 red by James Wong Howe. “A fusion of Hollywood genre with personal visio
 n … closer to poetry than pulp. Its sculptural weight can only be apprec
 iated on the big screen” (Amy Taubin\, Village Voice ).\nCategory: Films
 \nOriginal listing: https://events.berkeley.edu/BAMPFA/event/328110-film-s
 creening-raging-bull
LOCATION:BAMPFA\, BAMPFA
STATUS:CANCELLED
URL:https://events.berkeley.edu/BAMPFA/event/328110-film-screening-raging-
 bull
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:berkeley-arts
END:VEVENT
