BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:La maison des bois: Episodes 1–3 — Berkeley/San Francisco
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-07:00":20261017T140000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-07:00":20261017T150000
DTSTAMP:20261017T203942Z
UID:092d8e3fe93056303c398179e40c@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Films\,Berkeley/San Francisco\,United States
DESCRIPTION:Epic yet intimate\, sweeping yet personal\, La maison des bois
  stands as one of the greatest achievements in the history of television\,
  as well as legendary director Maurice Pialat’s magnum opus. Commissione
 d for Télévision Française in 1971\, this seven-episode\, nearly four-h
 undred-minute miniseries considers the impact of World War I on a simple F
 rench family living in the countryside. Applying a naturalistic focus to t
 heir subject\, Pialat and screenwriter René Wheeler capture both the hist
 orical scope of the conflict and the subtle ways that a small town’s quo
 tidian routines and rituals—church\, school\, tavern—are indelibly tou
 ched by it.\nCategory: Films\nOriginal listing: https://events.berkeley.ed
 u/BAMPFA/event/328113-la-maison-des-bois-episodes-13
LOCATION:BAMPFA\, BAMPFA
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://events.berkeley.edu/BAMPFA/event/328113-la-maison-des-bois-epi
 sodes-13
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:berkeley-arts
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:RIPCORD — Atlanta
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-04:00":20261017T143000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-04:00":20261017T170000
DTSTAMP:20261017T203942Z
UID:51223ae4a6593195a77fe41c084d@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Theater\,Atlanta\,United States
DESCRIPTION:A sunny room on an upper floor is prime real estate in the Bri
 stol Place Senior Living Facility\, so when the cantankerous Abby is force
 d to share her quarters with new-arrival Marilyn\, she has no choice but t
 o get rid of the infuriatingly chipper woman by any means necessary. A see
 mingly harmless bet between the old women quickly escalates into a dangero
 us game of one-upmanship that reveals not just the tenacity of these worth
 y opponents\, but also deeper truths that each would rather remain hidden.
  “Tastily sweet-and-sour\, Ripcord is great fun!” – Time Out New Yor
 k\nCategory: Theater\nOriginal listing: https://www.artsatl.org/event/ripc
 ord/2026-10-17/1/
LOCATION:Stage Door Theatre\, 5339 Chamblee Dunwoody Road\, Atlanta\, GA\,
  30338
