DTSTART;TZID="UTC-07:00":20261018T000000
DTSTAMP:20261017T203942Z
UID:b3dc033122a50920fa95f558f404@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Performing Arts\,Berkeley/San Francisco\,United
  States
DESCRIPTION:Created with students in the Spring 2026 Theater 114 Class Dir
 ected by Timmia DeRoy World Premiere! This brand-new play\, collaborativel
 y authored by Berkeley students in the spring of 2026\, brings us a slice-
 of-life look into the lives of Gen Z on and off campus. Inspired by real-l
 ife conversations and the subreddit Am I The Asshole? \, each vignette—f
 rom the raunchy to the heartfelt—creates surprising opportunities for se
 lf-reflection. A bit too close to home\, comedic\, and at times absurd\, T
 he Whole Shebang tackles messy and challenging topics through multiple per
 spectives\, offering an unfiltered experience and a mirror to our times. T
 his show discusses topics of political\, sexual and person\nCategory: Perf
 orming Arts\nOriginal listing: https://events.berkeley.edu/TDPS/event/3220
 94-tdps-presents-the-whole-shebang-chronicles-of-very-se
LOCATION:Durham Studio Theater\, Durham Studio Theater
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://events.berkeley.edu/TDPS/event/322094-tdps-presents-the-whole-
 shebang-chronicles-of-very-se
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:berkeley-arts
END:VEVENT
