BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Elizabeth Field and David Sariti - 400 Years of Music! — Washing
 ton\, DC
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-04:00":20261018T150000
DTSTAMP:20261017T203942Z
UID:2ef4b66756ba0314e30f2dffc33b@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Arts & Culture\,Washington\, DC\,United States
DESCRIPTION:Elizabeth Field and David Sariti: 2 Violinists\, 4 Violins\, 8
  Bows and 400 Years of Music! This wide-ranging program gives audiences a 
 rare opportunity to hear first-hand the evolution of the violin and its bo
 ws. Field and Sariti will guide the listener through time by explaining th
 e evolution in construction and how it mirrored changes in compositional a
 nd playing style. From early 17th-century consort music\, to the high Baro
 que\, domestic Classical music\, Romantic chamber music\, and concert piec
 es of the 20th and 21st centuries\, the listener will experience the equiv
 alent of four concerts in one!\nCategory: Arts & Culture\nOriginal listing
 : https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/elizabeth-field-and-david-sariti-400-year
 s-of-music
LOCATION:Flagg Building\, 500 17th Street NW\, Washington DC 20006
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/elizabeth-field-and-david-sariti-400-ye
 ars-of-music
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:gwu-arts
END:VEVENT
