DESCRIPTION:In this talk\, Professor of Practice of International Affairs 
 Robert Sutter will explore the past\, present\, and future of the relation
 ship between the Republic of China (Taiwan) and the United States. He will
  begin by explaining the lasting legacies over the last 100 years of the R
 epublic of China government on Taiwan. Since the first Trump administratio
 n\, the US has hardened its policies and attitudes toward the People’s R
 epublic of China (China)\, with Taiwan playing a critical role in such a p
 olicy. However\, recently\, uncertainty has entered into the US-Taiwan rel
 ationship due to domestic and international headwinds. In Taiwan\, an upco
 ming 2028 presidential election could result in a dramat\nCategory: Academ
