UID:faeecaa418dc3843eb54b83d7193@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Arts & Culture\,Washington\, DC\,United States
DESCRIPTION:The 1920s emerged as a decade suspended between collapse and r
 econstruction\, an era marked by “cracks and reforms” that ushered in 
 a profound reconfiguration of the visual world.  During this period marke
 d by civil transformation and political upheaval\, artists\, journalists\,
  and makers had opportunities to reconstruct both individual and collectiv
 e identities. A century later\, Cracks & Reforms presents a distinct cross
 -section of this period\, revealing global currents of migration\, moderni
 zation\, and cultural redefinition through the lens of the GW Collection. 
 Students led by Associate Professor Bibiana Obler selected works to study 
 and exhibit\, their research eventually leading to unified t\nCategory: Ar
 ts & Culture\nOriginal listing: https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/cracks-refo
 rms-the-1920s-through-the-gw-collection
