SUMMARY:How Democracies Revive: Why Illiberalism Keeps Winning and What to
  Do About It — Washington\, DC
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-04:00":20261021T160000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-04:00":20261021T170000
DTSTAMP:20261017T203942Z
UID:69b8ee862ea7b0a6246a68a297e3@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Academic\,Washington\, DC\,United States
DESCRIPTION:Despite occasional setbacks\, illiberalism keeps winning\, fro
 m India and the United States to Germany. Analytical frameworks remain pol
 arized among cultural backlash\, economic grievance\, and illiberal-playbo
 ok accounts. Each explains part of the picture\, but none captures the com
 prehensiveness of the illiberal challenge. This talk\, drawing on a forthc
 oming Stanford University Press book that blends scholarly research with i
 nsider political experience\, proposes a relational materialist framework.
  It traces illiberalism to the contradictions of an uneven and shifting hi
 erarchical global economic order\, which generate a triple devaluation of 
 economic status\, cultural worth\, and political voice t\nCategory: Academ
 ic\nOriginal listing: https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/how-democracies-reviv
 e-why-illiberalism-keeps-winning-and-what-to-do-about-it
LOCATION:Elliott School of International Affairs\, 1957 E St NW\, Suite 41
 2\, Washington\, DC 20052
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/how-democracies-revive-why-illiberalism
 -keeps-winning-and-what-to-do-about-it
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:gwu-arts
END:VEVENT
