 es
DESCRIPTION:The conversation around dementia is expanding beyond diagnosis
  and caregiving into prevention\, early detection\, and living well after 
 a diagnosis. This session explores the latest brain health research alongs
 ide the growing movement to build dementia-friendly communities\, challeng
 ing stereotypes and examining what a society-wide response looks like in b
 oth policy and practice. Speakers Tesha Coleman - Program Manager\, DC Bra
 in Health Jessica Fredericksen - Senior Director\, Goodwin Brain Health Be
 cca Levy - Professor of Epidemiology and Psychology\, Yale University Nanc
 y Nelson and Kat Hartley - Co-founders\, Dangle and Dot Scott Turner - Pro
 fessor and Director\, Georgetown University Memory Dis\nCategory: Communit
