SUMMARY:Presentation: Cosamala\, by Alana S. Portero — Madrid
DTSTART;TZID="UTC+02:00":20261024T213000
DTEND;TZID="UTC+02:00":20261024T213000
DTSTAMP:20261017T203942Z
UID:95c09ccbeaae60335a6d0b3422e4@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Multidisciplinary\,Madrid\,Spain
DESCRIPTION:Andalusia\, 1937. The Carranza column—composed of horsemen\,
  bullfighters\, Falangists\, landowners\, and Civil Guards—advances thro
 ugh the northern mountains of Seville\, subjugating everything in its path
  and drenching the land in blood\, like Death riding across the fields. A 
 group of women—wives\, mothers\, and neighbors of fugitives and the pers
 ecuted—initiate themselves in the dark language as a form of resistance
 \, forming a coven with the goal of bringing life back to an infertile cou
 ntry with the help of their dead and ghosts. Cosamala is a witch story tha
 t stems from a real Civil War crime and feeds on elements of horror and fo
 lklore to build its own female mythology of vengeance\, love\, and \nCateg
 ory: Multidisciplinary\nOriginal listing: https://www.mataderomadrid.org/e
 n/schedule/presentation-cosamala-alana-s-portero
LOCATION:Casa del Lector\, Plaza de Legazpi\, 8\, Madrid\, 28045
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://www.mataderomadrid.org/en/schedule/presentation-cosamala-alana
 -s-portero
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:europe
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:matadero-madrid
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Dynamic! – Funny scenes\, songs and games! — Atlanta
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-04:00":20261024T220000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-04:00":20261024T233000
DTSTAMP:20261017T203942Z
UID:4de1269babcd2c497789c81cd934@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Theater\,Atlanta\,United States
DESCRIPTION:The Dynamic! is an improv show that thrives on chaos\, quick t
 hinking\, and whatever ideas the audience throws at the cast. Every scene
 \, game\, and musical moment is built in real time\, and the performers le
 an into the unexpected with a mix of confidence\, silliness\, and genuine 
 surprise. They know how to turn a wild suggestion or a joke that goes off 
 the rails into something even funnier\, and half the joy is watching them 
 navigate the mess together. The show moves fast\, the energy stays high\, 
 and no two nights ever feel the same. You help spark the fun\, and the cas
 t runs with it to create a comedy experience that feels alive\, loose\, an
 d completely in the moment.\nCategory: Theater\nOriginal listing: https://
 www.artsatl.org/event/the-dynamic-funny-scenes-songs-and-games-5/2026-10-2
 4/
