DESCRIPTION:AI is transforming how energy technologies are discovered\, de
 signed\, operated\, and protected. Hosted by Johns Hopkins University\, th
 e AI-Enabled Energy Systems Conference will take place on Wednesday\, Oct.
  28\, and will bring together researchers from academia\, industry\, and g
 overnment to explore emerging research opportunities and challenges at the
  intersection of AI and energy. The conference will examine the role of AI
  across the energy ecosystem\, from scientific discovery and materials des
 ign to energy technologies and infrastructure\, system operations and reli
 ability\, and security and recovery. The morning session will feature invi
 ted talks and discussion across these areas. Jessica Gran\nCategory: Lectu
