UID:3043fb04b8868f1669be8fe65ee2@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Arts & Culture\,Washington\, DC\,United States
DESCRIPTION:In the 2010s\, Western documentary filmmakers gained access to
  a Russian real-estate oligarch\, Aras Agalarov\, and his son\, Emin. From
  this they made the film\, Breaking the West\, which explores the story of
  the Agalarov family and its ties to countries outside of Russia\, includi
 ng the United States. After screening this film\, Peter Baker\, Susan Glas
 ser\, Bridget Hunnicutt and Michael Kimmage will discuss its core themes
 \, from kleptocracy in Russia to international patterns of corruption and 
 influence peddling - past and present. .\nCategory: Arts & Culture\nOrigin
 al listing: https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/movie-screening-breaking-the-we
 st
