CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Books\,Atlanta\,United States
DESCRIPTION:Dr. Beverly J. Armento\, an Atlanta author and educator\, will
  moderate what is sure to be a lively discussion about Susan’s #1 New Re
 lease debut memoir\, The Earth Is Flat?! And Other Things My Mother Taught
  Me. Reserve your ticket now! This laugh-out-loud and vulnerable debut MOM
 oir is about a homeschooled Pentecostal girl in the ’90s\, her flat-eart
 her mother\, and the hilarious\, heartbreaking work of figuring out what
 ’s actually true. “Unputdownable” -The Santa Barbara Independent Sus
 an has appeared on Jane the Virgin\, The Mindy Project\, and hosts L.A. Th
 is Week. She earned her B.A. in Journalism and Dramatic Art from UNC-Chape
 l Hill and a Master of Sustainable Tourism from ASU.\nCategory: Books\nOri
 ginal listing: https://www.artsatl.org/event/author-talk-with-actor-and-au
 thor-susan-huckle/
LOCATION:Village Books\, 213 Mitchell St SW\, Atlanta\, 30303
STATUS:CONFIRMED
